From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Ocarina MME state fix: parked methods carry their macro state; macro restarts and
 non-macro methods reset a half-fed macro (captured from the working tree, 8 Nov 2026)

Until this patch these edits lived only in Eglantine/src (the PS5 build of ocarina-mme-state-fix
was made from them) and were not in the patch series, so a clean resync would have dropped them.

- ParkedMacro (split_macro_state.h): a method parked at a split entry takes the Maxwell3D / compute
  macro id, words, segments with it (Take/Restore), and gets them back when the stream resumes.
- A macro-start write (even method) for another macro, or a non-macro method, resets a half-fed macro
  in Maxwell3D (back and front) and KeplerCompute instead of appending to it / asserting.
- A failed native macro on the front no longer leaves draw_pending set.
- "Submission ended with an unparked method" is reset and logged.
- SplitContinuesHere shares ReadsAsCommands with split_macro_state.h.
- Ocarina (0400486024DEC000) defaults for EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_KEEP_FRAME, _INVALIDATION_FILTER,
  _SKIP_OVERWRITTEN_UPLOADS and _FLUSH_DRAWS=4096 when the variable is unset.
